Note: remove all prerequisites

Instruction

Your studies have made you an exceptional teacher. Over the course of 1 hour, which can be during a rest, you can grant a Humanoid proficieny in one skill, tool, or weapon that you are proficient in, or teach it to speak one language you know.

The knowledge lasts until the creature finishes a long rest.
Perfect Recall

You can recall picture-perfect details from anything that you commit to memory. If you spend at least 1 minute observing an object or creature, you can perfectly recall any observable information about it at any point in the future.

For example, you could memorize a map, one page from a book, a mysterious inscription, or a creature's appearance.
Quick Study

You learn exceptionally fast. Over the course of 1 hour, which can be during a short or long rest, you can gain proficiency in a skill or tool, or learn a language. You must have an example to learn from, such as a manual or a creature to teach you.

This knowledge lasts until you use this feature again.
Astrology

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You are a disciple of heavenly bodies and use this knowledge to twist fate. You gain proficiency in Arcana. If you are already proficient, then whenever you make an Arcana check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

During each long rest that you can see the night sky, roll a d20 and record the number. Once before the end of the next long rest, you can choose to use that roll in place of a d20 for an ability check, attack roll, or saving throw, before you roll.
Falconry

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You have learned to train birds of prey for scouting and use in combat. You gain proficiency in Perception. If you are already proficient, then any time you make a Perception check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

You also gain a trained Falcon that uses the following rules:

Statistics. The Falcon uses the Hawk stat block, but it has an Intelligence score of 8. You can communicate simple ideas with one another using only simple gestures and sounds.

Combat. The Falcon is unwaveringly loyal and acts during your turn in combat. It can move and its reaction on its own, but it only takes the Dodge action unless you use your bonus action to command it to take an action from its stat block, or another action. If you are Incapacitated, your Falcon can act on its own, and will defend you to the best of its abilities.

Death. If your Falcon falls to 0 hit points, it makes death saving throws as a player character would. Should it die, your unique skills allow you to track and train another Falcon over the course of an 8-hour period using 5 gold worth of bait.
Linguistics

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You are a student of language and the spoken word. You gain proficiency in Persuasion. If you are already proficient, then any time you make a Persuasion check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

You also learn to speak, read, and write bonus languages equal to your Intelligence modifier. Should your Intelligence modifier change, it changes the bonus languages you know.
Physical Fitness

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You know that the key to a healthy mind is a healthy body. You gain proficiency in Athletics or Acrobatics. If you are already proficient in that skill, then whenever you make a check with that skill, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

You also gain a climbing speed equal to your walking speed or a swimming speed equal to your walking speed.

You can learn this Scholarly Pursuit twice. However, you must choose different skills and speeds each time.
Riddles

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You have spent a great deal of time learning to speak in both riddles and rhymes. You gain proficiency in Deception. If you are already proficient, then whenever you make a Deception check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

Also, when you speak, you can choose to speak in Riddles. When you do so, you appear to be speaking normally, but you include hidden messages laced in your rhyming words.

Over the course of 1 hour, which can be during a rest, you can teach any creature with an Intelligence of 11 or higher to understand the secret messages contained in your Riddles.
Secrets & Whispers

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You know just where to eavesdrop. You gain proficiency in Stealth. If you are already proficient, then when you make a Stealth check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

Whenever you spend a long rest in a Settlement, you can spend 1-hour gathering local rumors to learn of a significant, even secret, event which occurred in there in the past week.
Theology

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You are a dedicated scholar of various holy texts and sacred ritualism. You gain proficiency in Religion. If you are already proficient, then any time you make a Religion check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

You also learn to speak, read, and write Celestial, and you learn the ceremony spell, but you can only cast it as a Ritual. For you, the Ritual only takes 10 minutes, and you can cast it without the material components once per long rest.
Traditions

Prerequisites: 4th-level Savant
You are a student of culture, politics, and traditions. You gain proficiency in History. If already proficient, when you make a History check, you can replace your d20 roll with your level.

Any time you make an ability check to interact with a local ruler or figure, you can make a History check in place of the normal skill, incorporating your knowledge of customs.